<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hun Sen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1952</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hun Sen is a Cambodian politician, a former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> commander who fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> in 1977 and returned with the Vietnamese invasion of 1979. He became foreign minister and in 1985 prime minister of the People's Republic of Kampuchea, continued in the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>, and after the 1993 settlement shared power before taking sole control in 1997. He governed until 2023, when his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hun-manet">Hun Manet</a> succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hun-sen.jpg" alt="Hun Sen" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: World Trade Organization from Switzerland (proccession made by Roman Kubanskiy) · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hun_Sen_July_2019.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
